From 9074cec1dd65fc9ed4b9f2d2b148f4327e40ba97 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vasilii Zolotukhin <vasilii.zolotukhin@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 10:25:18 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] Mac: pinned tabs in the unified strip

The tab menu's Pin Tab works now. The pinned tabs of all profiles come
first in the unified strip, as narrow tabs with just the icon and the
profile mark; in vertical mode they are tiles in rows above the other
tabs (one per row when collapsed), outlined like Chromium's.

As in a Chromium window, a tab that gets pinned goes after the pinned
tabs and one that gets unpinned before the others; dragging and the
move-tab keys keep pinned tabs among the pinned ones and the others
among the others.
